{
  "_README": [
    "Cost unit is wall-clock seconds on the target box, derived from throughput_items_per_sec.",
    "Model keys are UNVERIFIED placeholders. Workstream 5 replaces them from config.py once the",
    "real NIM/vLLM model strings are confirmed — a wrong string that looks right costs hours.",
    "scripts/calibrate.py rewrites the numbers and flips measurement_status to MEASURED.",
    "",
    "Three sections, because models do three different jobs and conflating them has caused",
    "the same bug three times. A predicate model answers a yes/no question about an item. A",
    "derivation model transforms data into a field that did not exist. A retrieval model",
    "ranks. Only predicate_models can be bound to a predicate, so 'transcription model bound",
    "to an AUDIO predicate' is no longer something this file can express."
  ],

